From: Andrea Pesaresi <andreapesaresi82@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: align MTK wireless control attribute IDs with mt76

mt76's mtk_vendor_attr_wireless_ctrl pins MTK_VENDOR_ATTR_WIRELESS_CTRL_CERT
to 9 (RTS_SIGTA therefore 10), while hostapd's copy of the enum lets CERT
fall to 8 and RTS_SIGTA to 9. hostapd does not emit either attribute today,
so the mismatch is latent, but any future SET of RTS_SIGTA from hostapd
would land on the driver's CERT slot and flip certification mode.

Pin CERT = 9 on the hostapd side too, matching the driver ABI.

Fork note: this is the src/common/mtk_vendor.h hunk of pesa1234's
999-002-fix-mtk-vendor-control-error-handling (577d51786a); the rest of
that patch (vendor dump hardening) is not taken.
---
 src/common/mtk_vendor.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/common/mtk_vendor.h
+++ b/src/common/mtk_vendor.h
@@ -181,7 +181,7 @@ enum mtk_vendor_attr_wireless_ctrl {
 	MTK_VENDOR_ATTR_WIRELESS_CTRL_BA_BUFFER_SIZE,
 	MTK_VENDOR_ATTR_WIRELESS_CTRL_MIMO,
 	MTK_VENDOR_ATTR_WIRELESS_CTRL_AMSDU,
-	MTK_VENDOR_ATTR_WIRELESS_CTRL_CERT,
+	MTK_VENDOR_ATTR_WIRELESS_CTRL_CERT = 9,
 	MTK_VENDOR_ATTR_WIRELESS_CTRL_RTS_SIGTA,
 
 	/* keep last */
